=== PREFIX LADDER (run level, the stated product) ===
1100 games with both starters modelled and a complete inning line

             sim   actual     diff      se   sigma  per inning
  F1        0.92     1.05   -0.127   0.046    -2.8      -0.127
  F3        2.74     2.87   -0.137   0.074    -1.8      -0.010
  F5        4.70     4.96   -0.263   0.096    -2.7      -0.126
  F7        6.57     6.88   -0.311   0.115    -2.7      -0.048

  'per inning' is the MARGINAL error this inning adds. A cumulative
  total drifts, so the marginal column is what localises the defect.

=== HEADROOM (starter discrimination, holdout, leash off) ===
  holdout: rates before 2026-07-01, starts on or after it, leash OFF
    300/520 games

  population: arms meant to go long, 1009 starts, 30 draws each

  stat     actual sd  between  ceiling  our corr   share  our spread
  outs          3.88     1.60    0.411     0.049     12%        0.86
  k             2.48     1.20    0.482     0.375     78%        1.02

  'our spread' is the sd of our per-start predicted means. It is
  the model's own differentiation, and it caps `our corr` however
  well aimed the predictions are.
  Leash OFF and rates frozen, so outs is a LOWER bound.
